oup with Mushroom · 30 Minutes · Japanese · ♥ (Photo_Chicken_Ramen)\n     - Instagram posts (01, in order): 1. Photo_Instagram_1 — \"The vegetable dishes need to have certain vitamins for those people\" 2. Photo_Instagram_2 — \"Sweet food can bring someone happiness, as long as they don't eat too much\" 3. Photo_Instagram_3 — \"What do you do before you start cooking? Prepare the tools or the ingredients?\" 4. Photo_Instagram_4 — \"Steak is never wrong; it's perfect if you want a romantic dinner\". All posts: Avatar_Foodieland · \"Foodieland.\" · \"Tokyo, Japan\" · more icon · photo counter 1/3 · like/comment/send/save icons · \"Liked by craig_love and 44,686 others\" · caption · \"September 19\"\n     - Recipe (02): Title \"Healthy Japanese Fried Rice with Asparagus\". Intro: \"A quick weeknight fried rice that turns leftover rice into a light, healthy meal. Crisp asparagus, soft eggs and a simple soy-sesame sauce come together in one pan in about 30 minutes.\" Meta: Avatar_John_Smith · John Smith · 15 March 2022 · PREP TIME 15 Minutes · COOK TIME 15 Minutes · Healthy. Nutrition: Calories 219.9 kcal · Total Fat 10.7 g · Protein 7.9 g · Carbohydrate 22.3 g · Cholesterol 37.4 mg · note \"Values are per serving and approximate.\" Ingredients — For main dish (5): \"2 cups cooked jasmine rice, chilled overnight\" (CHECKED) · \"1 bunch asparagus, cut into 2 cm pieces\" · \"2 eggs, beaten\" · \"2 spring onions, thinly sliced\" · \"1 tbsp neutral oil\"; For the sauce (3): \"2 tbsp soy sauce\" · \"1 tsp sesame oil\" · \"1 tsp mirin\". Directions: 1. \"Prepare the ingredients\" — \"Cut the asparagus, slice the spring onions and beat the eggs. Mix the soy sauce, sesame oil and mirin in a small bowl.\" + Photo_Cooking_Step + tip \"Day-old rice works best: it is drier, so the grains fry separately instead of turning mushy. Break up any clumps before you start.\" 2. \"Cook the eggs and asparagus\" — \"Heat the oil in a wok over high heat. Scramble the eggs until just set, push them to the side, then stir-fry the asparagus for 2 minutes until bright green and still crisp.\" 3. \"Fry the rice and season\" — \"Add the rice and toss for 3–4 minutes until hot and lightly toasted. Pour over the sauce, fold in the eggs and spring onions, and serve right away.\" Other Recipe (3, each photo + \"By Andreas Paula\"): Chicken Meatballs with Cream Cheese · The Creamiest Creamy Chicken and Bacon Pasta · The Best Easy One Pot Chicken and Rice. Actions: PRINT (Icon_Print), SHARE (Icon_Share). Video cover Photo_Japanese_Fried_Rice + Icon_Play.\n     - Articles (03, all dated 12 November 2021): 1. Crochet Projects for Noodle Lovers · Wade Warren (Photo_Chicken_Ramen, Avatar_Wade_Warren) — \"Our favourite slurpable noodle bowls, from quick ramen to slow-simmered broths.\" 2. 10 Vegetarian Recipes To Eat This Month · Robert Fox (Photo_Tropical_Fruit_Salad, Avatar_Robert_Fox) — \"Seasonal, meat-free dishes that are colourful, filling and easy to make.\" 3. Full Guide to Becoming a Professional Chef · Dianne Russell (Photo_Blog_Chef, Avatar_Dianne_Russell) — \"A working head chef on first jobs, long services and what it really takes.\" 4. Simple & Delicious Vegetarian Lasagna · Leslie Alexander (Photo_Vegetarian_Lasagna, Avatar_Leslie_Alexander) — \"Layers of roasted vegetables, rich tomato sauce and creamy béchamel.\" 5. Plantain and Pinto Stew with Aji Verde · Courtney Henry (Photo_Plantain_Stew, Avatar_Courtney_Henry) — \"A hearty one-pot stew finished with a bright, herby green sauce.\" 6. We're Hiring a Communications Assistant! · Albert Flores (Photo_Hiring, Avatar_Albert_Flores) — \"Love food and words? Join our small team and help us tell more food stories.\" Page intro: \"Blog & Article\" · \"Recipes, kitchen tips and stories from the Foodieland team.\" Search: \"Search article, news or recipe...\" + \"Search\". Tasty Recipes (sidebar, each \"By Andreas Paula\"): Chicken Meatballs with Cream Cheese (Photo_Chicken_Meatballs) · Traditional Bolognaise Ragu (Photo_Creamy_Chicken_Bacon_Pasta) · Pork and Chive Chinese Dumplings (Photo_Dumplings). Pagination: 1 · 2 · 3 · 4 · 5 · … · next (Icon_Chevron_Right), current = 1.\n     - Blog post (04): Title \"Full Guide to Becoming a Professional Chef\" · Avatar_Dianne_Russell · Dianne Russell · 12 November 2021. Intro: \"We asked a working head chef about first jobs, long services and what it really takes to make it in a professional kitchen.\" Photo_Blog_Chef. Q1 \"How did you start out in the food industry?\" — \"I started washing dishes in a small family restaurant when I was sixteen. Watching the line cooks every night made me want to be on the other side of the pass, and after two years the chef finally let me prep vegetables.\" Q2 \"What do you like most about your job?\" — \"The rhythm of service. Hours of preparation come down to a few intense minutes, and when a full dining room goes quiet because everyone is eating, it feels like the whole team has done something together.\" Q3 \"Do you cook at home on your days off?\" — \"Yes, but simply. I cook the food I grew up with: rice, eggs and whatever vegetables look good at the market. Home cooking is where I remember why I love food.\" [Photo_Cooking_Step after 3rd answer] Q4 \"What would your advice be to young people looking to get their foot in the door?\" — \"Start anywhere and be the person who shows up early. Ask questions, taste everything and write down what you learn.\" Pull quote (after Q4): \"Technique can be taught; curiosity and reliability can't.\" Q5 \"What is the biggest misconception that people have about being a professional chef?\" — \"That it is all creativity. Most of the job is consistency: making the same dish perfectly two hundred times a night, keeping the kitchen clean and looking after your team.\" Share: \"SHARE THIS ON:\" + 3 social logos. Recommended: \"Check out the delicious recipes\" + first 4 of More recipes.\n     - Newsletter (all 5 frames): \"Deliciousness to your inbox\" · \"Get ne