ep instance text as \"Button\"?? No — must say Subscribe/Search/Submit/View Recipes.\n\nTrick: setRangeFontName etc fine. What about setting textAutoResize on instance text? If I set text child to a fixed size with center alignment: child.resize(w=160?) — resize on text child of instance — likely also blocked. Test it.\n\nIf blocked: Option B: overlay approach — place the given button instance, then place MY OWN text on top? Ugly duplicate (button's own text still visible saying \"Button\"). Could set characters to spaces \"        \"? Then overlay real text centered manually (my text node on page, not in instance). That preserves \"reuse\" (the button component IS used for the visual) and gives perfect centering. Hacky but effective and safe. Button text color white — overlay text white too.\n\nActually simpler: set instance text characters to the real string; if x can't move, compute expected visual offset: text x stays fixed at original position (left edge fixed). Original \"Button\" width 51 centered in 160 → x=54.5. \"Subscribe\" at 15-16px Medium ~ 75 wide → occupies 54.5..129.5, center 92 vs 80 → off by 12px. Noticeable but minor? For \"Search\" (~52px) fine. \"View Recipes\" ~95. Off-center by ~10-14px. Meh.\n\nTry the resize approach in a test call first — quick read+write test on a throwaway instance... Write test: create btn instance, try children[0].resize(160,60) and .x=0 in try/catch, report which succeed, then remove instance. That's cheap. If resize allowed: set text width to button width + align CENTER + x=0 → perfectly centered. If x blocked but resize allowed, set textAlignHorizontal='CENTER' with full width — text centers within its box.\n\nLet me run that test plus read TextField/button geometry details in one read/write-light call (creates temp instance on page 9:2, then removes it — no residue).\n\nAlso same for field instance: test Input resize + Placeholder x/y/resize; test Label visibility.\n\nThen rebuild Call 1 with corrected approach.","