NTER, primaryAxisAlignItems CENTER), child = my own TEXT (Inter Medium 16 white). Instances: override characters → auto-recentered. This is a \"reusable Button\" built ON the given Button's design language... but brief says \"Reuse the provided Button and Text Field components\". Hmm. The safest compliance: USE given button instances for all primary buttons AND fix centering.\n\n  Trick 10: Test if bt.constraints is settable. If yes, use Trick 7 with resize dance. Constraints on instance children — I think constraints ARE readable but not writable on instance children (they're fixed by component). Likely FAIL.\n\n  Trick 11: What about setting bt.characters AND bt.fontSize to shrink/grow? No.\n\n  Trick 12: Put the label as a range with letterSpacing to adjust total width to 51? E.g. 'Subscribe' at fontSize 16 w77 — need 51: impossible.\n\n  Trick 13: textAutoResize='NONE' + resize(160,60) + x stays 54.5 → box 54.5..214.5, then set textAlignHorizontal='CENTER' → visual text centered at 134.5. Then... resize the INSTANCE to 289 wide so button spans 0..289 and text center = 134.5+27.5? No wait: box center fixed at 134.5 relative to instance left; if instance width = 269, center = 134.5 ✓. So instance width 269 → text perfectly centered, but button is 269 wide not 160. For wide CTAs (e.g., 200+), could work... but our buttons are 160.\n\n  OK — decision: use Trick 11-style overlay: given Button instance + set its text to '' + overlay my own centered text node directly on the page frame (sibling above). For prototype clicks, set reaction on both instance and overlay text. This uses the given component for every CTA (visual = component), satisfies reuse, and centering is exact. The only quirk: my text nodes aren't part of the instance — acceptable.\n\n  Wait — but can I even set bt.characters=''? Should be fine.\n\n  Hmm, actually one more: maybe constraints ARE writable on instance children. Quick test in next call (cheap): set bt.constraints; catch. If OK, do the resize dance (161 then 160) and verify bt.x recenters. I'll test in the build call and fall back to overlay automatically. Actually simpler to just test now quickly? Each call costs time; I'll integrate conditional logic into the build: try constraints route; if fails, overlay route. Complexity risk... Let me just do a fast targeted test now to decide cleanly.\n\n- Field: Input resize OK, hideLabel OK, setPl OK. Input y=29 fixed (label hidden leaves 29px gap at top — transparent since label hidden). So: instance 420×89 with input at y29. In newsletter: place fld.y = 136-29 = 107. Input resize(420→ keep 420? plan 372). resizeInput OK → inp.resize(372,64)? h60 keep 60. So inp.resize(372,60). Placeholder pl stays at x25,y21 within Input — vertically centered in 60 ✓. \n- Label: I could also reuse labels: for contact form, override label characters (allowed) — label stays at y0, input at y29 — perfect structure: label above input. Label font 14 Medium; override via setRangeFontName to Semi Bold 12 + ls 4%? setRange on instance text allowed (setChars OK). fontSize override via setRangeFontSize allowed. Good.\n- Input stroke exists: #DBE2E5-ish (0.8588,0.886,0.898 = #DBE2E5). Good for focused state: override inp.strokes to black 2px.\n\nButton test: constraints writable?","signature":"91ea74091f1243a5a81bd71a"}],"id":"a2c7154c-c4f2-408c-8772-3572a3679990","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed01e25d-1512-4496-b486-8851c6325863","uuid":"9cd10c07-251d-4a0e-b385-00a3415961b4","timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:35:57.915Z","thinking_duration_ms":57151}
