for 3–4 minutes until hot and lightly toasted. Pour over the sauce, fold in the eggs and spring onions, and serve right away.'; Other Recipe (3, 'By Andreas Paula'): Chicken Meatballs with Cream Cheese/meat · The Creamiest Creamy Chicken and Bacon Pasta/pasta · The Best Easy One Pot Chicken and Rice/onepot; PRINT (Icon_Print) · SHARE (Icon_Share); video cover rice + Icon_Play; recommended heading 'You may like these recipes too' + first 4 of More recipes (trop fav, wagyuA, rice, cauli)\n     - Blog (03): 'Blog & Article' · 'Recipes, kitchen tips and stories from the Foodieland team.' · search 'Search article, news or recipe...' + 'Search'; Articles (all 12 November 2021): 1 Crochet Projects for Noodle Lovers/Wade Warren/aWad/ramen/'Our favourite slurpable noodle bowls, from quick ramen to slow-simmered broths.' 2 10 Vegetarian Recipes To Eat This Month/Robert Fox/aRob/trop/'Seasonal, meat-free dishes that are colourful, filling and easy to make.' 3 Full Guide to Becoming a Professional Chef/Dianne Russell/aDia/blogChef/'A working head chef on first jobs, long services and what it really takes.' 4 Simple & Delicious Vegetarian Lasagna/Leslie Alexander/aLes/lasagna/'Layers of roasted vegetables, rich tomato sauce and creamy béchamel.' 5 Plantain and Pinto Stew with Aji Verde/Courtney Henry/aCou/plantain/'A hearty one-pot stew finished with a bright, herby green sauce.' 6 We're Hiring a Communications Assistant!/Albert Flores/aAlb/hiring/'Love food and words? Join our small team and help us tell more food stories.'; Tasty Recipes ('By Andreas Paula'): Chicken Meatballs with Cream Cheese/meat · Traditional Bolognaise Ragu/pasta · Pork and Chive Chinese Dumplings/dump; Pagination 1·2·3·4·5·…·next (chevR), current=1\n     - Blog post (04): 'Full Guide to Becoming a Professional Chef' · Dianne Russell · 12 November 2021 · intro 'We asked a working head chef about first jobs, long services and what it really takes to make it in a professional kitchen.' · Photo_Blog_Chef; Q1 'How did you start out in the food industry?' — 'I started washing dishes in a small family restaurant when I was sixteen. Watching the line cooks every night made me want to be on the other side of the pass, and after two years the chef finally let me prep vegetables.' Q2 'What do you like most about your job?' — 'The rhythm of service. Hours of preparation come down to a few intense minutes, and when a full dining room goes quiet because everyone is eating, it feels like the whole team has done something together.' Q3 'Do you cook at home on your days off?' — 'Yes, but simply. I cook the food I grew up with: rice, eggs and whatever vegetables look good at the market. Home cooking is where I remember why I love food.' + Photo_Cooking_Step after Q3; Q4 'What would your advice be to young people looking to get their foot in the door?' — 'Start anywhere and be the person who shows up early. Ask questions, taste everything and write down what you learn.'; pull quote 'Technique can be taught; curiosity and reliability can't.'; Q5 'What is the biggest misconception that people have about being a professional chef?' — 'That it is all creativity. Most of the job is consistency: making the same dish perfectly two hundred times a night, keeping the kitchen clean and looking after your team.'; 'SHARE THIS ON:' + 3 socials; 'Check out the delicious recipes' + first 4 of More recipes\n     - Contact (05): 'Contact us' · NAME ('Enter your name...') · EMAIL ADDRESS ('Your email address...') · SUBJECT ('Enter subject...') · ENQUIRY TYPE: Advertising (chevD) · MESSAGE ('Enter your message...') · 'Submit' · Photo_Chef_Contact · 'Check out the delicious recipes' + first 4 of More recipes\n   \n   - **PROTOTYPE LINKS (required)**: 01: fried rice card → 02; nav Blog → 03; nav Contact → 05. 02: nav Home → 01; nav Blog → 03. 03: article 'Full Guide to Becoming a Professional Chef' → 04; nav Home → 01. 04: nav Blog → 03; recommended fried rice card → 02. 05: nav Home → 01; recommended fr